---
import { systemGuidelines } from '../data/system-guidelines';
const { contrasts, outline, offset, target } = systemGuidelines();
---
<section id="accessibility" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Accessibility</h2><p>Keep content readable, controls named and keyboard focus visible.</p></header>
  <h3>Text contrast</h3><p>Ratios include alpha text over the actual surface. Primary and secondary text pass AA for normal text. Accent is not a general body-text colour; check its size and background before using it for text.</p>
  <div class="ds-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Text</th><th>Background</th><th>Light</th><th>Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{contrasts.map(pair => <tr><th><code>{`--${pair.foreground}`}</code></th><td><code>{`--${pair.background}`}</code></td>{pair.themes.map(result => <td>{result.ratio}:1 · {result.normalTextAA ? 'AA for normal text' : 'Below AA for normal text'}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Focus and targets</h3><p>The shared focus outline is <code>{outline}</code>, with an offset of <code>{offset}</code>. Controls keep a minimum target of <code>{target} × {target}</code>, including invisible padding where the visible control is smaller. Inline links within prose retain their inline treatment.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard and media</h3><p>Use native links, buttons and inputs. Keep visible labels or accessible names. Escape, the close button and browser Back return focus to the project card. Keep meaningful image alternatives, video controls and captions with the media.</p>
  <h3>Reduced motion</h3><p>Content stays available without entrance motion. Icon rain and repeating decoration stop. Case studies open and close without travel. Videos use their still image until the reader chooses to play.</p>
</section>
<section id="writing" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Writing</h2><p>Put the purpose first. Use short, concrete labels and sentences.</p></header><ul class="ds-principles"><li>Name the destination or action. Case-study project links use “Website”.</li><li>Keep project names, outcomes and supplied claims in their original context.</li><li>Keep the supplied dates and durations; do not calculate new timeline copy.</li><li>Keep supporting notes with their metrics. Do not turn a supplied claim into a measured result.</li><li>Use the supplied tool names as accessible labels. Do not add captions or slogans.</li></ul><details class="ds-implementation"><summary>Implementation</summary><p>These rules follow the portfolio copy notes and the shared project-link convention.</p></details></section>
